# .trivyignore — vulnerabilities deferred for triage
#
# Add a line per CVE ID to suppress that finding from the Trivy SCA scan
# (security-fast.yml job: trivy-fs). Lines starting with # are comments.
# Empty lines are ignored.
#
# Format examples:
#   CVE-2024-12345                     # suppress everywhere
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31      # suppress until expiry, then re-fail
#
# When suppressing a CVE, leave a one-line note explaining *why* — typically:
#   - Vendor patch not yet released and the affected codepath is unreachable.
#   - False positive: dependency is dev-only / test-only.
#   - Vendor disputed: link to the vendor advisory rejecting the CVE.
#
# Each entry needs an owner and an expiry. Without those, suppressed CVEs
# decay into invisibility and the security posture quietly weakens.
